  "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
  "body": "Hi,\na 3 line instructions is as follows (assuming you have all the dependencies in place):\n\n```\n$ mkdir build; cd build; cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release ..\n$ make -j$(nproc) install\n$ cd Release/ART.app; python ../../../tools/osx/bundle_ART.py -o /tmp -v -r /opt/local/lib -n\n```\n\nThis should create an app bundle in `/tmp/ART.app`.\n\nAlternatively, you can fork the project and use the existing github actions (from \"Actions -> macOS Builds -> Run workflow\") to create a dmg. I didn't try but it should work.",
